Z||000000||pontiacs4me||03-06-2001||08:53 PM||||Ok, today Im driving around and my windshield wipers turn on mysteriously again.  this time it had nothing to do with the turn signal, I was just driving straight.  I pushed the squirter switch and it turned off after 2 more swipes.  About 2 miles later it did it again.  this time it didnt turn off.  Any position I put the wiper switch in it goes the same speed and the only way to turn it off is to un plug it.  What is the deal here?  Not to mention that the belt is squalling and the brake light is on again, and it is making a bonging sound and the speakers are popping, Im going be wearing a straight jacket soon, this thing is about to put me in a loony bin.||||reg||1
Z||000001||stsmithgt||03-07-2001||09:53 AM||||Mine did that.  I went to the bone yard and picked up another controller board that goes in the front of the wiper motor.  Popped out the old one and put in the other and it hasn't done it since.  It might only be damp?  It's a pretty primitive looking circuit board even with mechanical switches on it. Yuk.  Those cures may not be the problem.  The banging around on it might of fixed it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
